{"version":"1","id":"erlangforums","handle":"erlangforums","name":"Erlang Forums","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/b352c25bf0ad4af3b186d4cdf1c4f17c","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-3.0815,"y":-3.5554,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":303,"newest_post_at":"2026-04-28T16:30:58.000Z","oldest_post_at":"2024-04-26T13:00:02.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.00495,"listicle_ratio":0.0033,"question_ratio":0.006601,"avg_read_time":2.069307,"summary_length_avg":379.613861,"title_length_avg":55.105611,"title_length_var":345.137361,"tag_entropy":2.797956,"tag_diversity":0.280528,"top_tag_share":0.254125,"avg_upvotes":0.234323,"median_upvotes":0.0,"avg_comments":0.0,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.013889,"zero_engagement_share":0.854785,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":2.896955,"non_article_ratio":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":0.122222},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-7.5,-7.0441],"cadence_depth":[6.0588,-7.5588],"hype_variety":[-1.5147,-3.8824],"title_style":[-2.7059,0.3971]},"top_tags":[["erlang",282],["authentication",61],["functional-programming",42],["security",39],["tech-news",23],["elixir",22],["distributed-systems",22],["ssh",19]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["RabbitMQ\u2019s Common Issues & Misconceptions: A Support Perspective - Johan Rhodin","RabbitMQ Summit 2024 - Learning Resources / Talks - Erlang Forums","Erlang OTP-27.1 Released"],"outlier":["Maybe and when"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"zPpXSgYV9","title":"Lambda Days - Learning Resources / Talks - Erlang Forums","url":"https://erlangforums.com/t/your-docs-are-a-program-zainab-ali-lambda-days/5591","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/lambda-days---learning-resources-talks---erlang-forums-zppxsgyv9","summary":"A talk from Lambda Days 2025 exploring the idea that documentation is fundamentally a program. It draws parallels between doc pipelines and programming pipelines, covering phases, symbols, and errors unique to documentation. The talk surveys tools like Pollen in Racket, Elixir Livebooks, and mdoc/Laika in Scala to envision what an ideal documentation language could look like, aiming to improve developer workflows and inspire custom doc tooling.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--VDukGCjf--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2002","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-28T16:30:58.000Z"},{"id":"hZnvl5mU4","title":"Lambda Days - Learning Resources / Talks - Erlang Forums","url":"https://erlangforums.com/t/what-is-functional-programming-adam-warski-lambda-days/5589","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/lambda-days---learning-resources-talks---erlang-forums-hznvl5mu4","summary":"A talk from Lambda Days 2025 by Adam Warski exploring what functional programming actually means. It covers how to visually identify functional code, generalizes intuitions about FP features (from higher-order functions to capturing effects as values), introduces different FP flavors to explain why definitions vary, and attempts to rank which FP features bring the most value while measuring mainstream languages by their 'functionfullness'.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--VDukGCjf--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2002","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-28T16:28:54.000Z"},{"id":"m154jTlqh","title":"Lambda Days - Learning Resources / Talks - Erlang Forums","url":"https://erlangforums.com/t/testing-functional-uis-hayleigh-thompson-lambda-days/5587","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/lambda-days---learning-resources-talks---erlang-forums-m154jtlqh","summary":"A talk from Lambda Days 2025 by Hayleigh Thompson on testing functional UIs, shared on the Erlang Forums under the Code Sync talks collection.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--OHB84bZF--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2010","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-28T16:24:24.000Z"},{"id":"JGb5OwVxU","title":"Haskell is Eating my Rails App from the Inside Out - Brian Carroll","url":"https://erlangforums.com/t/haskell-is-eating-my-rails-app-from-the-inside-out-brian-carroll-lambda-days/5586","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/haskell-is-eating-my-rails-app-from-the-inside-out---brian-carroll-jgb5owvxu","summary":"A Lambda Days 2025 talk by Brian Carroll about incrementally replacing a Ruby on Rails application with Haskell, migrating from an object-oriented web framework to a functional programming language from the inside out.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--P4t4XyoV--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2001","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-28T13:00:03.000Z"},{"id":"1chJA7dRA","title":"Lambda Days - Learning Resources / Talks - Erlang Forums","url":"https://erlangforums.com/t/you-dont-need-an-orm-giacomo-cavalieri-lambda-days/5584","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/lambda-days---learning-resources-talks---erlang-forums-1chja7dra","summary":"A talk from Lambda Days 2025 by Giacomo Cavalieri arguing that ORMs are unnecessary, presented at the Code Sync conference series. The content advocates for an alternative approach to database access without relying on object-relational mapping layers.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--OHB84bZF--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2010","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-27T22:53:39.000Z"},{"id":"F1M9POBA6","title":"Why Clojure and Datomic Excel in Real-World Systems - Jordan Miller","url":"https://erlangforums.com/t/why-clojure-and-datomic-excel-in-real-world-systems-jordan-miller-lambda-days/5582","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/why-clojure-and-datomic-excel-in-real-world-systems---jordan-miller-f1m9poba6","summary":"A Lambda Days 2025 talk by Jordan Miller exploring why Clojure and Datomic are well-suited for real-world production systems. The post is a forum thread linking to the talk with minimal additional context.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--foaA6JGU--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2004","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-27T22:52:14.000Z"},{"id":"UJFOz0GhE","title":"Lambda Days 2025 - Learning Resources / Talks - Erlang Forums","url":"https://erlangforums.com/t/hoogle-for-the-hungry-masses-farhad-mehta-lambda-days-2025/5581","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/lambda-days-2025---learning-resources-talks---erlang-forums-ujfoz0ghe","summary":"A talk by Farhad Mehta from Lambda Days 2025 titled 'Hoogle for the Hungry Masses!' is shared on the Erlang Forums under the Code Sync talks collection. The post invites community comments and links to related Code Sync conference talks.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--1KxV4ohY--/f_auto/v1722860400/public/Placeholder%2007","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-27T22:24:35.000Z"},{"id":"M2AKprm3T","title":"Lambda Days 2025 - Learning Resources / Talks - Erlang Forums","url":"https://erlangforums.com/t/painting-with-functions-in-cyfra-szymon-rodziewicz-lambda-days-2025/5580","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/lambda-days-2025---learning-resources-talks---erlang-forums-m2akprm3t","summary":"A Lambda Days 2025 talk by Szymon Rodziewicz introduces Cyfra, a DSL and compiler that allows writing functional Scala code which compiles to SPIR-V and runs on GPUs via a Vulkan runtime. The talk demonstrates building a 3D ray tracing and ray marching renderer entirely in functional Scala, and explores using Cyfra for animations and GPU-accelerated compute in business applications.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--1KxV4ohY--/f_auto/v1722860400/public/Placeholder%2007","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-27T22:24:05.000Z"},{"id":"iHOLMsMQ7","title":"Patch Package OTP 28.5 Released","url":"https://erlangforums.com/t/patch-package-otp-28-5-released/5570","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/patch-package-otp-28-5-released-iholmsmq7","summary":"Erlang/OTP 28.5 patch release includes updates to four applications: erl_interface-5.7, erts-16.4, mnesia-4.25.3, and ssl-11.6. Key changes include a new Secure Coding Guidelines document for Erlang, a new configure option for managing embedded third-party dependencies (zstd, zlib, openssl, etc.), bug fixes in enif_make_map_from_arrays for maps with 33+ keys, Unicode handling fix for erl.exe on Windows, Mnesia transaction stacktrace fix, and TLS-1.3 certificate selection conformance fix.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--foaA6JGU--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2004","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-23T15:28:02.000Z"},{"id":"cSh8rUijz","title":"Patch Package OTP 26.2.5.20 Released","url":"https://erlangforums.com/t/patch-package-otp-26-2-5-20-released/5565","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/patch-package-otp-26-2-5-20-released-csh8ruijz","summary":"Erlang/OTP 26.2.5.20 patch release fixes two bugs: a Unicode handling issue in erl.exe on Windows when using the args_file option (erts-14.2.5.14), and a security vulnerability (CVE-2026-32147) in the SFTP server where FSETSTAT operations on open file handles could modify file attributes outside the configured root directory, bypassing chroot boundary restrictions (ssh-5.1.4.15).","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--foaA6JGU--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2004","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-21T11:11:17.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["linkedin","github_updates","chromium","ch9","begin"],"opposite_handles":["dailydevworld","horde","on_leuwcq","watercooler","dotnetsquad"],"similar":[{"id":"linkedin","handle":"linkedin","name":"LinkedIn Engineering","is_squad":false,"x":-2.7252,"y":-3.6286,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":300,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/le","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.892355,"median_upvotes":0.0,"author_present